# Solarus runtime flag OVERRIDES — sourced by solarus_run.sh whenever this file
# EXISTS (the old second key, SOLARUS_ALLOW_DIAG_ENV=1, was removed 2026-07-19).
# End-user protection is now by ABSENCE: deploy.py removes this file on every
# deploy UNLESS run with --diag. To force it off without deleting it, launch with
# SOLARUS_NO_DIAG_ENV=1.
#
# HW-validated perf/correctness levers are ENGINE DEFAULTS (ON without any env var):
# SOLARUS_TILERESIDENT (#56), SOLARUS_FASTPACE (#54/55), SOLARUS_AUDIO_THREAD (#55),
# SOLARUS_IDLEPARK (#59), SOLARUS_BGPLANE (#121), SOLARUS_OVERLAY (#125).

# ===========================================================================
# STAGE 2 — sprite channel (OP_SPRITELIST) validation session
# ===========================================================================
# BOTH lines are REQUIRED to get any Stage 2 data. With SPRITECH unset the session
# measures the DEFAULT path and every counter below reads as though the feature did
# not exist — which looks exactly like a clean pass. Do not skip either.

SOLARUS_BLITTER_DIAG=1     # per-60fr [blitter*] banners -> /media/fat/logs/Solarus/Solarus.diag.log
SOLARUS_SPRITECH=1         # enable the sprite channel (engine default is OFF)

# SPRITECH semantics (mister_flag_default_off): absent -> OFF, =0 -> OFF, =1 -> ON.
# Unlike the older presence-based flags in this engine, `SOLARUS_SPRITECH=0` really
# does disable it — commenting the line out and setting =0 are equivalent.

# --- What to read out of Solarus.diag.log --------------------------------
# [blitter diag]  sprite_blits=  individual camera-surface blits (the SPRITECH-off path)
#                 tile_blits=    batched tile entries + bgplane plane COPYs
#                 dropped=       ring commands LOST to overflow (must be 0)
#                 spr_rec=       sprites buffered into the channel
#                 spr_runs=      OP_SPRITELIST commands emitted
#                 spr_drop=      sprites refused at the cap / SP_BUF full (want 0)
#                 cmdcnt=        ring commands for the last frame
# [blitter inter] used=          INTER arena occupancy (sizing evidence for Stage 3)
#
# The collapse ratio is spr_rec / spr_runs. Report the MEASURED ratio — the plan's
# estimate is not evidence. Expect N -> few, not N -> 1: a run breaks whenever
# stride/format/blend/alpha/colorkey/flags change.
#
# A/B: capture the same scene at SOLARUS_SPRITECH=1 and =0. Sanity check is
# spr_rec (on) ~= sprite_blits (off) — the same sprites routed a different way.
# The sprite cap is chosen FROM this census; do not carry forward a guessed number.

# --- #122 / #123 scroll-transition A/B (folded into this session) ---------
# Uncomment for the overlay axis of the 2x2. Scroll targets: overworld map 8 to_B1
# -> map 9, to_A2 -> map 10; map 9 to_C1 -> map 3. Simplest repro is walking off a
# screen edge in the overworld.
# The TITLE SCREEN CANNOT test either issue — with no previous map
# g_transition_scroll is never true, and it has no tile layers so the bgplane hold
# frame is structurally impossible. A clean title screen proves nothing.
# Stage 2 is gated behind !g_transition_scroll, so this A/B measures the SOFTWARE
# fallback, not the sprite channel. Worth running (Stage 1's claim to have fixed
# both was never verified) but do not attribute the result to Stage 2.
# SOLARUS_OVERLAY=0          # force the overlay channel OFF for the A/B

# --- other diagnostics (extra perf cost + log spam) -----------------------
# SOLARUS_BGPLANE_DIAG=1     # per-bake ARM/BAKE/EMIT census (needs BGPLANE on)

# --- opt-outs (uncomment to disable a HW-validated default for an A/B) ----
# SOLARUS_BGPLANE=0          # force the per-layer plane bake OFF
# SOLARUS_BGPLANE_SYNC=0     # legacy one-cell-per-frame bake (default is synchronous load-time)
# SOLARUS_TILERESIDENT=0
# SOLARUS_FASTPACE=0
# SOLARUS_AUDIO_THREAD=0
# SOLARUS_IDLEPARK=0
